<title>USA: SPX says to repurchase shrs, end dividends.</title>
<headline>SPX says to repurchase shrs, end dividends.</headline>
<dateline>MUSKEGON, Mich. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>SPX Corp said it adopted a new financial strategy that includes a &quot;Dutch auction&quot; repurchase tender offer commencing April 11 for 2.7 million shares at $48 to $56 per share.</p>
<p>The company also said future distributions are expected to be made through share repurchases and quarterly cash dividends are eliminated.  </p>
<p>&quot;The new strategy aligns the company's financial and capital policies with the Economic Value Added financial management system that has been the basis of its performance measurement and compensation systems since early 1996,&quot; SPX said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
